{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794014829,"nonce":"Mr5puPO1jfhPkJgPLpC6FyoYkVo=","message":"Implemented in e487f833e1638dfc1982b66efe5d21e15d46b974 (local, not pushed): shards read the stream with LLVMGetBitcodeModuleInContext2 and a small C++ bridge (cpp/lazy_bodies.cpp: Function::materialize, Function::deleteBody). The emitter now decides the carried small bodies once; a shard materializes owned and carried bodies and drops the rest unread. ASH_AOT_EAGER_PARSE=1 is the old path.\n\nMeasured on the Mac, wasm32-wasip1-threads, 6 shards, AIR cache warm, release builds, outputs byte-identical to v0.1.16 in every run (same SHA-256), also under ASH_AOT_EAGER_PARSE=1 and --no-air-cache, and for the thread-throw program. Machine not quiet (1-minute load 3-10).\n- 61 MB stream (RayDE explorer-interactions.hl, 11,601 bodies), 3 interleaved runs each: shard prepare 7.2-8.0 s -\u003e 1.0-1.1 s; wall 40.7/38.7/37.6 s -\u003e 38.3/30.2/31.8 s; peak RSS 3.69-3.93 GB -\u003e 2.67-2.70 GB.\n- Demo-sized (RayDE cc-lifecycle.hl, 2.06 MB bytecode, 20.9 MB wasm), scripts/bench_wasm_compile.py, codegen level 0, fibers, 3 runs: shard prepare median 2238 -\u003e 542 ms; middle end 2823 -\u003e 2807 ms and codegen 1112 -\u003e 1165 ms unchanged; wall median 11.5 -\u003e 10.0 s; CPU median 36.3 -\u003e 29.2 s.\nTests: aot_shard unit tests 4/4 including a lazy-read test; aot_smoke and thread_throw pass. Not run: the NUC (it ran out of memory building ash; Linux numbers unmeasured), a program with wasm traps/exceptions beyond thread_throw, aot_dynamic_throw (needs Haxe).","files":null}]}